---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CTABlock from '../components/CTABlock.astro';
import { breadcrumbSchema, personSchema } from '../lib/schema';
import { LOCATION } from '../lib/site';

const path = '/about';

const schema = [
  personSchema(),
  breadcrumbSchema([
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'About', path },
  ]),
];
---

<Base
  title="About Taylor Corbett — Sonora"
  description="Fifteen years across newsrooms, state government communications, and B2B software content strategy. Now running content and search strategy independently."
  path={path}
  schema={schema}
>
  <article class="section page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <img
        src="/images/taylor-corbett.webp"
        alt="Taylor Corbett, founder of Sonora"
        width="520"
        height="520"
        fetchpriority="high"
        decoding="async"
        class="headshot"
      />

      <div class="prose about-body">
        <h1>I&rsquo;ve spent fifteen years figuring out what people are looking for.</h1>

        <p class="lead">
          I started in television news. The job there was to know what a
          community would search for before they knew they&rsquo;d search for it
          &mdash; a shooting, a school closure, a hurricane, a store that might be
          open. You wrote the thing people needed and you wrote it before they
          asked. That is still the entire job, and everything since has been a
          variation on it.
        </p>

        <p>
          From there: digital director for a network affiliate, running a team of
          producers and the audience strategy behind them. Press relations for a
          state agency, where the work was getting a specific message into
          publications that had no obligation to carry it. Communications for a
          technology company most people have in their pocket. Then several years
          running the entire content function for a B2B software company &mdash;
          strategy, editorial, search, measurement, and the reporting that went to
          the board.
        </p>

        <p>
          That last role is where the current problem became obvious. We were
          producing good work and ranking well, and increasingly it didn&rsquo;t
          matter, because a growing share of buyers were never seeing a results
          page at all. They asked a model and took the answer. So I built a
          measurement program to find out what those models were saying about us
          and about our competitors, and the answers were not flattering, and
          fixing it turned out to be a different discipline than SEO.
        </p>

        <p>Sonora is that discipline, run as a practice.</p>

        <h2>How I work</h2>

        <p>
          I&rsquo;m one person. That&rsquo;s deliberate. You get senior judgment
          on every decision instead of a partner in the pitch and an associate on
          the work.
        </p>

        <p>
          I set strategy and direction. I don&rsquo;t write your blog posts or
          build your site &mdash; your team or your contractors do that, and I make
          sure what they produce is worth having made. If you need someone to
          execute, I&rsquo;ll tell you honestly and help you find them.
        </p>

        <p>
          I&rsquo;d rather tell you something uncomfortable in month one than let
          you spend a year on the wrong position.
        </p>

        <h2>Where I am</h2>

        <p>
          A ranch in the {LOCATION}, with two Australian shepherds who contribute
          nothing to the work but are on most calls.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <CTABlock />
</Base>

<style>
  .page-hero {
    padding-block: clamp(48px, 6vw, 80px) clamp(56px, 7vw, 96px);
  }

  .headshot {
    width: min(520px, 100%);
    height: auto;
    aspect-ratio: 1;
    object-fit: cover;
    border-radius: 260px 260px 2px 2px;
    margin-bottom: clamp(40px, 5vw, 64px);
  }

  .about-body h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 4.6vw, 3.5rem);
  }

  .about-body .lead {
    margin-top: 32px;
  }

  .about-body h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 2.6vw, 2rem);
  }
</style>
